{% comment %}
  To-scale size guide. The single biggest reason people do not buy a mirror online
  is that they cannot picture how big it is. Raw "73x52 cm" on a button does not
  answer that; a 170 cm person standing next to it does.

  Drawn as inline SVG rather than an uploaded image so it stays sharp at any size,
  follows the brand tokens, costs no extra request, and cannot go out of sync with
  the product.

  The SVG user unit IS one centimetre. viewBox 0 0 300 218 means a 3 m wide wall,
  with the floor at y=200 and label room underneath. To place anything, y = 200 minus
  its height above the floor. Do not "adjust until it looks right": change the
  centimetres and the drawing stays honest.

  Console: 120 cm wide, 80 cm tall, a normal hallway console.
  Mirror hangs with its base 95 cm from the floor, just clear of the console top.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign guide = ''
  case product.handle
    when 'brook-champagne-gold-wall-mirror', 'brook-matte-black-wall-mirror'
      assign guide = 'brook'
    when 'solenne-champagne-gold-full-length-mirror'
      assign guide = 'solenne'
  endcase
-%}

{%- if guide != blank -%}
<div class="sizeguide">
  <div class="sizeguide-head">
    <span class="option-label">Size in the room</span>
    <span class="sizeguide-note">Drawn to scale beside a 170 cm person</span>
  </div>

  <svg class="sizeguide-svg" viewBox="0 0 300 218" role="img"
       aria-labelledby="sizeguide-title sizeguide-desc">
    <title id="sizeguide-title">{{ product.title }} shown to scale</title>
    <desc id="sizeguide-desc">
      {%- if guide == 'brook' -%}
        A 170 cm tall person stands beside a 120 cm wide console table. The medium mirror
        measures 73 cm tall by 52 cm wide and the large mirror 90 cm tall by 65 cm wide,
        both hung with the base 95 cm above the floor.
      {%- else -%}
        A 170 cm tall person stands beside the Solenne mirror, which is 170 cm tall and
        90 cm wide and leans against the wall on the floor.
      {%- endif -%}
    </desc>

    <defs>
      {%- comment -%}
        The asymmetric silhouette, normalised to a 100x100 box so it can be dropped in at
        any real size. Deliberately a schematic outline, not a tracing of the product.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <symbol id="munler-blob" viewBox="0 0 100 100" preserveAspectRatio="none">
        <path d="M58 1 C84 4 99 26 94 52 C90 76 70 99 44 97 C20 95 2 74 3 48 C4 22 28 -2 58 1 Z" />
      </symbol>

      {%- comment -%}
        Built from primitives, not one path, because the geometry has to be provably
        full-height. The figure's bounding box must be exactly 0 to 160: the crown of
        the head at y=0 and the soles at y=160. Anything less and the figure floats,
        the scale silently lies, and the drawing is worse than no drawing.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <symbol id="munler-person" viewBox="0 0 46 160">
        <circle cx="23" cy="11" r="11" />
        <rect x="14" y="25" width="18" height="47" rx="8" />
        <rect x="5.5" y="29" width="7" height="42" rx="3.5" />
        <rect x="33.5" y="29" width="7" height="42" rx="3.5" />
        <rect x="15" y="70" width="7" height="90" rx="3.5" />
        <rect x="24" y="70" width="7" height="90" rx="3.5" />
      </symbol>
    </defs>

    <!-- floor -->
    <line class="sg-floor" x1="0" y1="200" x2="300" y2="200" />

    <!-- person: 170 cm tall, feet on the floor -->
    <use href="#munler-person" class="sg-person" x="24" y="30" width="49" height="170" />
    <text class="sg-dim" x="82" y="196">170 cm</text>

    {%- if guide == 'brook' -%}
      <!-- console: 120 cm wide, 80 cm tall -->
      <g class="sg-console">
        <rect x="112" y="120" width="120" height="5" />
        <rect x="118" y="125" width="4" height="75" />
        <rect x="222" y="125" width="4" height="75" />
        <rect x="118" y="180" width="108" height="3" />
      </g>

      <!-- large: 90 tall x 65 wide, base 95 cm up -> y 15..105, centred on x=172 -->
      <use href="#munler-blob" class="sg-mirror sg-mirror--large" x="139.5" y="15" width="65" height="90" />
      <!-- medium: 73 tall x 52 wide, base 95 cm up -> y 32..105 -->
      <use href="#munler-blob" class="sg-mirror sg-mirror--medium" x="146" y="32" width="52" height="73" />

      <text class="sg-label sg-label--large" x="212" y="24">Large &#183; 90 &#215; 65 cm</text>
      <text class="sg-label sg-label--medium" x="212" y="46">Medium &#183; 73 &#215; 52 cm</text>
      <text class="sg-dim" x="112" y="214">120 cm console</text>
    {%- else -%}
      <!-- Solenne: 170 tall x 90 wide, standing on the floor -->
      <use href="#munler-blob" class="sg-mirror sg-mirror--large" x="150" y="30" width="90" height="170" />
      <text class="sg-label sg-label--large" x="248" y="110">170 &#215; 90 cm</text>
      <text class="sg-dim" x="150" y="214">Leans against the wall</text>
    {%- endif -%}
  </svg>

  <p class="sizeguide-fit">
    {%- if guide == 'brook' -%}
      <strong>Medium</strong> sits comfortably above a console or in a cloakroom.
      <strong>Large</strong> is the statement piece, above a fireplace or on an empty wall.
    {%- else -%}
      Leans against the wall, no fixings needed. Give it about 90 cm of clear floor width.
    {%- endif -%}
  </p>
</div>
{%- endif -%}
